 ### TensoRF
-Uses vector-matrix decomposition for static 3D volumes. HexPlane extends this by adding temporal planes to handle 4D dynamic scenes. [TensoRF](3026-tensorf.md)
-*   **K*-Planes:** Also employs six feature planes for representation. HexPlane is most closely related to this method. [K*-Planes](link_not_provided)
-*   **DyNeRF:** Uses implicit MLPs and per-frame latent codes. HexPlane is >100× faster and uses less memory (200MB vs implicit models). [DyNeRF](link_not_provided)
+Uses vector-matrix decomposition for static 3D volumes. HexPlane extends this by adding temporal planes to handle 4D dynamic scenes. Choose TensoRF for static scenes; choose HexPlane for dynamic scenes requiring explicit spatiotemporal factorization. [TensoRF](3026-tensorf.md)
+
+### K*-Planes
+Also employs six feature planes for representation. HexPlane is most closely related to this method. Choose K*-Planes for n-dimensional generalizations; choose HexPlane for standard 4D dynamic novel view synthesis. [K*-Planes](link_not_provided)
+
+### DyNeRF
+Uses implicit MLPs and per-frame latent codes. HexPlane is >100× faster and uses less memory (200MB vs implicit models). Choose DyNeRF for deformation-heavy monocular videos; choose HexPlane for speed and memory efficiency without deformation fields. [DyNeRF](link_not_provided)
 
